<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},
<p>Thank you for contacting the Qantas Customer Care team.<br />
<br />
<strong>We're working as hard as we can to get you on your way</strong><br />
We’re sorry we had to cancel <strong>&lt;Flight no.&gt; </strong>because of <strong>&lt;insert reason&gt;</strong>. We’ve done our best to get you on your way again today, but we will always put safety before schedule.</p>

<p><b><i>If delay within QF control use:</i></b></p>

<p>If you’ve paid for accommodation and meals out of pocket, we’ll reimburse you $200 AUD per room for accommodation and $50 AUD per person for meals, and cover reasonable transfer costs.<br />
Qantas will consider claims for all costs caused by the delay or cancellation on a case by case basis, including claims for higher amounts where reasonably incurred.<br />
For further information, please refer to our <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/book-a-trip/flights/compensation-and-refunds-policy.html#:~:text=Claiming%20a%20refund,booked%20for%20the%20travel%20taken.">Compensation and Refunds page</a>.</p>

<p><b><i>If cancellation or delay due to weather or air traffic control use:</i></b><br />
<br />
<strong>Things don’t always go to plan</strong><br />
We’re committed to getting you to your destination on time, however, bad weather, natural disasters, technical problems and other issues can cause flight delays and cancellations, and your safety is our first priority.<br />
Though this delay was out of our control, I can understand how frustrating it must have been.<br />
<br />
<strong>We're here to help</strong><br />
While this disruption was outside our control and we’re unable to reimburse you for unexpected expenses such as accommodation. However, if you have travel insurance please let us know if you require an insurance letter to confirm details of your trip.</p>
